erhero film turning  any and all apparent theatrical or  ostentatiousness from the original  comics run all the way up to 11. this  film is bonkers with a capital silent q  i know i normally break down these kinds  of films based on their narrative or  creative merits but i feel like doing so  with this film would do a disservice to  this magnificent work of art and indeed  all of you for instance the first 10  minutes of this film acts as a quick  introduction to what exactly we'll be  getting ourselves into for the following  104 minutes it does not pull its punches  in being exactly what you might think it  is we get a pole to the batcave that  dresses them up in their iconic albeit  cheap looking crime-fighting costumes we  have the batmobile which produces fire  out the back that clearly isn't doing  anything there's the back copter which  is clearly a regular helicopter with bat  paraphernalia haphazardly strewn across  it and to my surprise we even get a  fleeting glimpse of batman's famed shark  repellent spray which naturally blows up  a shark  now before i go ahead and ignore the  plot of this film for the next three  minutes i'll quickly explain for those  of you who haven't seen this work of art  batman and robin try to stop the riddler  joker catwoman and penguin from doing  something evil for about 104 minutes  with some of the loosest applications of  logic i've ever witnessed in my life  there's a clear and concerted effort  made to make this some of the most  harmless television available while also  trying to deal with romantic  relationships kidnapping entanglements  hostage situations and a host of other  incredible circumstances for instance a  little over halfway through this film in  an effort to surprise attack batman  penguin dehydrates his minions into dust  and once inside the bat cave rehydrates  them however something goes wrong with  even the slightest touch the rehydrated  minions flash out of existence and the  following is batman's e