mic-con for batman and  robin i always apologize for that  speaking as someone that started this  video with virtually no basis or  knowledge of the batman series and spend  countless hours researching reading  watching and writing about them over the  last month so that i can apply it to  these films i can safely say that for  this film it has been an enormous waste  of my time for example poison ivy is a  character that plays a leading role in  this film and in preparation for her i  dedicated some time to try to figure her  out by consuming this short but  brilliant comic from 1986 called poison  ivy secret origins this was the comic  that redefined the character from her  campy golden age era persona into the  tragic heroine she's known as today and  furthermore this is a comic book that  understands and has a passion for the  character written by someone that could  take the perspective of a convicted  murderer of a psychopath and accurately  and charitably convey her perspective  for us not only to understand but also  connect with like check out this page  for example on this page our point of  view character steward asks poison ivy  why she's chosen her name to be poison  ivy the name of a weed when she herself  admits to having a passion for all  things botanical her response is concise  but illuminates so much about her as a  character she says there's no such thing  as a weed a weed is just a plant some  human decides is growing in the wrong  place  what an outstanding life this is what it  looks like when a writer is talented and  cares about these characters it's why we  look to passionate people online for  their takes on these things they love  because through these people we can see  these stories and characters in a new  light and none of that nuance or  interest is in this movie instead we get  bat nipples and close-ups of george  clooney's perfect ass and speaking of  george clooney one upsetting thing about  this film for me was that george clooney  was in the role of batman and not  because i don't like george clooney i'm  actually a fan of his work the  descendants and fantastic mr fox are  great films in their own right and oh  brother where art though happens to be  one of my favorite films of all time so  let me be clear i like me some clooney  but this script is not only broken on a  narrative level but totally misses the  point of batman's character that the  last film managed to get right to some  extent so in short this film makes me  hate george i always apologize for that  any hint of struggle or trauma behind  batman's eyes have been replaced by some  cheeky smirks and about 30 different dad  jokes if there's anything this last  month of reading and studying batman has  taught me it's that following the  facelift the series received in the 80s  all the best characters in the story are  ones rooted in or tangentially connected  to some sort of personal trauma batman  poison ivy dick grayson riddler catwoman  penguin heck the only one who isn't  directly tied to a trauma is the joker  and something must have happened to that  dude for him to turn out the way that he  was this is a story rooted in reality  and dark subject matter and this film  threw all of that out the window in  favor of what killed the dinosaurs  the ice age  iceman was an utter disaster of a  character and shared no resemblance to  his comic or animated series  counterparts for that matter reduced to  a single muscle-bound overly glitzy  laughable series of ice puns and look i  know this movie was geared towards  children but through iceman's ice  capades in this movie all it did was  leave me isolated as a viewer but look  it's no problem and okay i would try to  cram one more ice bun in here but it  slipped my mind so let's move on unlike  the prior film where i had my issues but  was able to find some positives this  film strips the story of any semblance  of weight or value for me it makes  batman worse dick grayson even more  annoying and filled itself with villains  that are either insulting or intolerable  and this film technically has bane by  the way a character that's supposed to  be a genius in both body and mind  someone that's famous for being the one  who broke the bat in both body and  spirit not some mindless zombie that's  pumped full of weird steroid stuff i  can't imagine what this film must have  been like for fans of batman back in the  day but right here and right now i'm  giving this disaster of a movie one out  of ten i really did not like any part of  this film and that does it those are all  the live-action batman films from before  the millennium quite the journey but  we're not even halfway yet next week i  have seven more films to review catwoman  2004 the nolan trilogy bvs joker and  justice league and my team won't let me  see anything other than the four-hour  schneider cut off the justice league  this is going to be a long week but  until then i've been totally not marked  i hope to see you all there same bad  time same bad place  [Music]  you
 

